-- title:
--   Conditioned lift descending to its trace algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a finite index type $n$, a topological group $G$, and a commutative local ring $\mathcal{O}$ with finite residue field, and work in the category $\mathrm{ProartinianCat}\,\mathcal{O}$ of local pro-Artinian topological $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with residue field that of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $F$ be a subfunctor of the functor [`Deformation.repnFunctor n G 𝓞`](def/Deformations_LiftFunctor.html#L18) sending an object $A$ to the continuous monoid homomorphisms $G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(A)$ and a morphism to pushforward of representations. Assume $F$ is conjugation-stable, i.e. $\gamma \bullet \rho \in F(A)$ whenever $\rho \in F(A)$ and $\gamma$ lies in `conjKer A`, the preimage under `ConjAct.ofConjAct` of the kernel of $\mathrm{GL}_n(A) \to \mathrm{GL}_n(k)$; and that $F$ is reflected by injective morphisms, i.e. for $\iota : T \to A$ with injective underlying map, $\sigma \in F(T)$ as soon as the pushforward of $\sigma$ lies in $F(A)$. Let $A$ be an object, and $\rho' : G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(A)$ continuous with $\rho' \in F(A)$ satisfying `TraceAlgebra.Descends`: some $\gamma \in$ `conjKer A` makes every matrix entry of every $(\gamma \bullet \rho')(g)$ lie in `traceSubalgebra 𝓞 ρ'`, the topological closure of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the traces of $\rho'$. Then there is a continuous $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_n\bigl(\mathrm{TraceAlgebra.obj}\ \rho'\bigr)$, over that closed trace subalgebra regarded as an object of the category, with $\sigma$ in $F$ of that object, with `traceSubalgebra 𝓞 σ = ⊤`, and whose pushforward along the inclusion `TraceAlgebra.ι ρ'` has the same class as $\rho'$ in $(\mathrm{repnQuotFunctor}\ n\ G\ \mathcal{O}).\mathrm{obj}\ A$, the quotient of representations by the conjugation action of `conjKer A`.
--
--   This is the conditioned form of the "descended element" step in the deformation-theoretic set-up of Mazur and Carayol: a representation satisfying a deformation condition and conjugate into its trace algebra admits a strictly equivalent model over that trace algebra, which satisfies the same condition and is topologically generated by its own traces. It is used in the proof of corepresentability of the conjugation-quotient subfunctor, [`Deformation.isCorepresentable_conjQuotSubfunctor_of_descends`](thm.html#Deformation.isCorepresentable_conjQuotSubfunctor_of_descends).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_exists_cond_lift_traceAlgebra.lean

import Mathlib
